    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP relies heavily on **Corbin Carroll** (82.69) and **James Wood** (78.42) today, as both occupy the premier spots in our daily tactical alignment. **Corbin Carroll** thrives against the soft-tossing Andre Pallante, benefiting from a high-efficiency environment where his elite speed is bolstered by the pitcher's slow delivery, effectively weaponizing his stolen base upside. Similarly, **James Wood** is in a smash spot against Jacob Lopez; with a league-leading 0.433 xwOBA and a prime leadoff assignment, he is positioned to capitalize on a favorable park factor and a weak opposing arm, making him a high-floor, high-ceiling anchor for our Roto points.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the staff was the exclusion of **Austin Riley** (44.86) from the starting nine. While he remains a core component of our roster, his matchup against Eovaldi presented an efficiency ceiling too low to justify displacing current starters. We opted instead to maximize our stolen base potential in the MI and OF slots, relying on the speed-heavy profiles of **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero** to pad our lead in the scarcest category. **Mickey Moniak** (64.11) also provides significant value; despite facing a tougher arm in Greene, his massive park factor bump and platoon advantage make him a superior start to the stationary bench options.\n\nWe are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for most of our squad, which introduces a layer of volatility for players like **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**. While both project well (61.84 and 64.04, respectively), any late-scratches or defensive shifts in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to **Henry Bolte** (48.02) if he hits the top half of the order. Investors should note that **Dalton Rushing** is currently our most fragile start (40.20) due to his low batting order placement and a daunting matchup against Schlittler; he is the most likely candidate to be bypassed if a better waiver opportunity arises before first pitch.",
